    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` and wrote 36 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. Line net is `unit_price × qty`, less the line discount, then the 5% standard bulk discount for qty ≥ 10 multiplied on top, rounded half-up to cents. Line tax is rounded per line, and the totals, credit handling and `tax_by_rate` are built from those rounded line values as the spec describes. Every validation rule in the spec raises `ValueError`, and the tests cover the boundaries (discounts of 0 and 100 allowed, a `bool` or float qty rejected, and so on). One choice the spec did not settle: I round the supplied credit to cents on entry, so a sub-cent credit is treated as its rounded value. I did not create any files beyond the two specified and installed nothing.",
